      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve  $y=2{x}^{2}+8x$ at the point $(2,24).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+8x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}+8x)=4x+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(2)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2)=4(2)+8=16\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=16$ and the coordinates of our point $(2,24),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(24) & =16(x-2) \\\\ y & =16x-32+24 \\\\ y & =16x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
